# Theme Color Modes

Climaybe helps AIs **use existing `_styles` when matching Figma**. It does **not** scaffold `_styles` from Figma. Token names, tones, and axes differ per theme. Discover them in **this repo** before writing markup. Names in this file are **illustrative**.

Do **not** treat any theme’s Figma collection catalog as shared SSOT. Theme-local notes (for example `theme-tokens.mdc`) are optional later — not this always-on rule.

## 1. Discover first

Before any color, size, or component class, grep **this theme**:

1. `_styles/` for `@utility` / `color-schema-*`, brand classes, `@theme` size overrides, semantic roles, atoms.
2. `layout/theme.liquid` and `_layout/theme.liquid` for brand classes on `<html>` and documented mode wrappers.

```bash
rg -n "@utility|color-schema|brand-|max-w-|--background-color|--text-color|--border-color|@theme|a--button" _styles/ layout/ _layout/ snippets/
```

Use only names that exist here. Do not copy another theme’s catalog.

## 2. Axes are optional

### Brand-on-`<html>`

Apply a brand class on `<html>` **only if** this theme ships Brand modes **and** a brand class (grep `_styles/` / `theme.liquid`). One class rebinds Brand CSS variables for the tree. Do not put brand on the section. Do not invent `brand-*` when none exist.

### Section tone

Tone list = **intersection** of Figma color modes and `@utility color-schema-*` (or this theme’s equivalent) **present in `_styles/`**. Never a fixed six-name list.

Some themes ship `color-schema-accent-1|2|3` — that is **one valid discovered pattern**, not “older only.” Other themes ship different tone names. Use what grep finds. Do not invent a missing `color-schema-*`.

Put the matching mode class on the **section root**. Children use semantic roles only.

## 3. Semantic roles

Roles = what `_styles` defines under the active schema (background / text / border utilities). Never hex. Never invent a missing role. Never emit Brand ramps (`color/neutral/*`, `color/accent/*`, `color/brand/*`) or primitive scales as Liquid classes.

If Figma names a role this theme does not ship, use the closest **existing** semantic utility. Do not add tokens from Figma.

## 4. Sizes

`_styles/02_base/*sizes*` (or this theme’s equivalent) is authoritative. Figma `02.01` layers may **override stock Tailwind** (`max-w-*`, `px` / `py` / `gap` / `height` / `icon` / `text-size`) via `@theme` / `@utility`. **Do not assume stock Tailwind values.** Grep first.

Map Figma `lg` | `md` | `default` → `lg:` | `md:` | base **only when this theme’s CSS remaps exist**. Never hard `px`.

## 5. Components → atoms

When this theme has component tokens (`03.01` / `03.02` or equivalent), they map to **atoms** (`a--button`, inputs), not invented `button/height` utilities. Build UI with existing atom classes / `{% render 'a--button', ... %}`. If no matching atom exists, compose from shipped semantic utilities — do not invent component utilities or hex.

## Mode first

1. Discover (grep above).
2. Set **brand** on `<html>` only when that axis exists.
3. Set **tone** on the section root from the intersection of Figma modes and this theme’s `color-schema-*`.
4. Children: semantic roles only. Buttons/inputs: atoms when present.

Then read `figma-design-system.mdc` and `tailwindcss-rules.mdc`.

## Forbidden

- Arbitrary hex / rgb: `text-[#d1d1d1]`, `bg-[#fff]`
- Inventing tokens or utilities that do not exist in `_styles/`
- Liquid-built class names: `text-{{ color }}`
- Brand ramps or primitive scales as Liquid classes
- Assuming stock Tailwind `max-w-*` / spacing when `02_base/*sizes*` overrides them
- Baking any theme’s Figma collection catalog (tone lists, brand verticals, role laundry lists) as shared SSOT
- Scaffolding `_styles` from Figma

## Illustrative only

```liquid
<section class="color-schema-muted">
  <div class="bg-surface text-primary border-secondary">
    <h2 class="text-primary">…</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary">…</p>
    {% render 'a--button', variant: 'primary', size: 'base' %}
  </div>
</section>
```

Replace every class / param with what this theme’s `_styles/` and atoms actually define. If grep found a brand class, set it on `<html>` — not on the section.
